{\pard\sa200\b\fs28 2. Two real bugs found running the trace (not staged — found live)\par}
\par
\pard Running the actual trace surfaced two genuine production defects that no amount of boot-log-reading had caught:\par
\par
\pard { Bug 1 — TLS cert never reached the deployed build.} We'd committed Supabase's root CA certificate to fix a TLS trust gap, but {1 tsc} only compiles {1 .ts} files — it silently never copied the {1 .crt} asset into the deployed {1 dist/} output. Every real database query was crashing with {1 self-signed certificate in certificate chain}, invisibly, because our own boot log only checks that the DB connection string parses, not that a query succeeds. Fixed the build step, verified against our own database before redeploying.\par
\par
\pard { Bug 2 — Supabase network restriction blocked our own server.} Our database has an IP allow-list (a deliberate hardening step from 2026-09-02). Our Railway production server's egress IP wasn't on it. Fixed by allow-listing it — flagging honestly that this is not a durable fix: Railway doesn't guarantee that egress IP stays stable without a paid static-IP feature we haven't enabled yet, so this could silently break again on a future redeploy. Tracked as a follow-up on our side, not blocking anything today.\par
\par
\pard Both fixed, redeployed, and reverified live before proceeding.\par
